{"file":"Clawness-1.18.0-v2.zip","bytes":686810,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"clawness","displayName":"Clawness","description":"Puts the right rules in context on every prompt, automatically — built for full-stack developers moving across frontend, backend, and SQL in one session, researchers working in bare or LaTeX-only directories, and teams who want adversarial review (security red/blue team, code critic) before merge. 222 rules across 30 domains, retrieved by relevance rather than dumped into CLAUDE.md, plus a plan-approval gate, session security hardening, and per-codebase lessons memory. Requires Python 3.10+ on PATH.","version":"1.18.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/fullymiddleaged/clawness","homepage":"https://github.com/fullymiddleaged/clawness","keywords":["rules","retrieval","rag","security","code-review","testing","performance","multi-agent","plan-mode","best-practices","science","research","llm"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/add/SKILL.md","name":"add","description":"Create a new Clawness rule from a natural language description. Describe what you want enforced and this will generate the YAML rule file with proper tags, triggers, and examples.","headings":["Create a New Rule","Process","Example"],"name_hint":"add","description_zh":"根据自然语言创建Clawness规则，生成包含标签、触发条件和示例的YAML文件。"},{"path":"skills/audit-rules/SKILL.md","name":"audit-rules","description":"Review one domain of the Clawness rule corpus for correctness against current official documentation, then record what was established as a version stamp (applies_to / verified / sources) on each rule individually. For maintainers and fork maintainers. Reports verdicts and writes stamps; never rewrites rule text.","headings":["Audit a rule domain","Before you start","Steps","1. Read the whole domain","2. Look up what is current","3. Give each rule a verdict","4. Report, don't rewrite","5. Stamp each rule individually","6. Verify","Don't"],"name_hint":"审查 · 规则","description_zh":"面向维护者逐域审查Clawness规则与当前官方文档的一致性，在每条规则记录applies_to/verified/sources版本标记，报告判断但不改写规则正文。"},{"path":"skills/bootstrap/SKILL.md","name":"bootstrap","description":"Author a starter set of Clawness rules for a project whose stack Clawness ships no corpus for (Ruby, PHP, Elixir, Haskell, C#, Swift, Dart, Scala, Clojure, ...). Researches the stack's current conventions from official documentation, drafts a small set of project rules into .clawness/rules/, lint-validates them, and stops for approval before writing anything. Run it when the SessionStart empty-coverage note fires, or whenever you want project rules for an uncovered stack.","headings":["Bootstrap rules for an uncovered stack","Argument","Steps","1. Establish what the project actually is","2. Look up current conventions — from documentation, not memory","3. Draft a SMALL starter set","Generated by /clawness:bootstrap for Haskell on <YYYY-MM-DD>.","4. Report the list and stop","5. Write the approved rules, then validate","Don't"],"name_hint":"bootstrap","description_zh":"为Clawness尚无规则库的技术栈研究官方约定、起草少量项目规则并lint验证；列出建议并在写入前停止等待批准，适用于覆盖为空提示或新技术栈。"},{"path":"skills/claude-md/SKILL.md","name":"claude-md","description":"Shrink an oversized CLAUDE.md. Measures what the project's always-loaded instructions cost per turn, then works through it section by section — cutting what the codebase already says, moving path-specific guidance to .claude/rules/ and prompt-specific conventions to .clawness/rules/, and leaving load-bearing \"don't undo this\" content where it is. Destructive and deliberate: run it when you have the session to spend.","headings":["Shrink CLAUDE.md","First: is this the right tool?","What actually reduces per-turn cost","Steps","1. Measure","2. Classify every section","3. Move one section at a time, verify, then delete","4. Finish","Don't"],"name_hint":"claude · md","description_zh":"精简过大的CLAUDE.md，测量逐轮常驻指令成本，删除代码已有说明，将路径专属和提示专属指导分移至相应规则目录，保留关键禁止撤销约束；属于有意的删除修改。"},{"path":"skills/eval-set/SKILL.md","name":"eval-set","description":"Build and run a project-specific retrieval eval so changes to your rules or base prompt are scored, not eyeballed. Mirrors tests/ground_truth.json + `clawness eval`: you write prompt→expected-rule cases, then measure MRR@k and hit-rate before and after an edit. Run it after trimming a base prompt into ranked retrieval (see openclaw-audit / claude-md), or whenever you change rules and want proof retrieval still surfaces what matters.","headings":["Score your retrieval, don't eyeball it","When to run it","Steps","1. Create the case file","2. Write good cases","3. Run it","4. Interpret and act on misses","5. Gate it (optional)","Don't"],"name_hint":"评测 · set","description_zh":"创建运行项目专属检索评测，编写提示到预期规则案例，比较改动前后MRR@k和命中率，验证规则或基础提示精简后重要知识仍可检索。"},{"path":"skills/openclaw-audit/SKILL.md","name":"openclaw-audit","description":"Trim an OpenClaw workspace's base system prompt. Measures what the always-injected workspace files (SOUL.md, AGENTS.md, IDENTITY.md, USER.md, MEMORY.md) cost per turn, then works through them section by section — cutting what the tools or codebase already say, moving durable conventions to Clawness ranked retrieval (.clawness/rules/) and one-line traps to .clawness/memory.md, and leaving load-bearing persona and identity where they are. Destructive and deliberate: run it when you have the session to spend.","headings":["Trim an OpenClaw workspace prompt","First: is this the right tool?","What actually reduces per-turn cost","Steps","1. Measure","2. Classify every section","3. Move one section at a time, verify, then delete","4. Finish","Don't"],"name_hint":"openclaw · 审查","description_zh":"精简OpenClaw常驻系统文件，测量SOUL/AGENTS/IDENTITY/USER/MEMORY逐轮成本，移出可检索惯例和简短陷阱，保留关键人格身份；属于有意的删除修改。"},{"path":"skills/perf/SKILL.md","name":"perf","description":"Run a performance audit on the project or a specific module. Checks for N+1 queries, unnecessary re-renders, memory leaks, bundle size issues, and slow algorithms.","headings":["Performance Audit","Steps"],"name_hint":"perf","description_zh":"审计项目或指定模块性能，检查N+1、不必要重渲染、内存泄漏、包体积及慢算法。"},{"path":"skills/refresh/SKILL.md","name":"refresh","description":"Bring this project's Clawness rules up to date with the framework version it actually runs. Establishes what is installed and what the codebase uses, looks up what changed since the rules were verified, and writes version-corrected overrides into .clawness/rules/ — reporting the list and stopping for approval before it writes anything. Run it when the SessionStart version-gap note fires, or whenever a major upgrade lands.","headings":["Refresh rules for a framework version","Argument","Steps","1. Establish what is actually installed","2. Establish what the codebase actually uses","3. Look up what changed","4. Classify each rule in the domain","5. Report the list and stop","6. Write the approved overrides","Generated by /clawness:refresh for Next.js 17 on <YYYY-MM-DD>.","7. Verify","Don't"],"name_hint":"refresh","description_zh":"依据项目实际安装使用的框架版本更新Clawness规则，研究验证后变化并准备版本正确的覆盖项，列清单后先等待批准再写入。"},{"path":"skills/review/SKILL.md","name":"review","description":"Run an adversarial code review on staged changes or a specific file. Spawns the code-critic agent to find bugs, performance issues, and missed edge cases. Use before merging PRs or committing.","headings":["Adversarial Code Review","Steps"],"name_hint":"评审","description_zh":"对暂存变更或指定文件开展对抗式代码评审，委派code-critic发现缺陷、性能与遗漏边缘情况，用于提交或合并前。"},{"path":"skills/security-audit/SKILL.md","name":"security-audit","description":"Run a stateful red team / blue team security audit on the current project or a specific module. First enumerates the attack surface deterministically with `clawness scan` (zero LLM tokens, identical every run) and accumulates verdicts in a findings ledger, so each pass adjudicates only what is NEW instead of re-scanning blind — turning a 5-10 run scan into 1-2 converging passes. Reach for this whenever the user asks for a security audit, a vulnerability scan, a code security review, or hardening — before deployment, after adding auth/ payment/user-data code, or on a schedule — even if they don't type the command.","headings":["Security Audit Workflow","Steps","Honest framing (state this, don't oversell)"],"name_hint":"安全 · 审查","description_zh":"对项目或模块开展有状态红蓝队安全审计，先用确定性clawness scan枚举攻击面，再累积发现台账，仅评估新增事项以收敛，适用于上线前或认证支付用户数据修改后。"},{"path":"skills/status/SKILL.md","name":"status","description":"Show the current Clawness configuration: which rules are loaded, which agents are available, and how the hook is configured. Use to understand what rules Claude is seeing for this project.","headings":["Clawness Status","Steps"],"name_hint":"status","description_zh":"展示当前Clawness加载规则、可用代理及钩子配置，了解项目向Claude提供了哪些规则。"},{"path":"skills/test/SKILL.md","name":"test","description":"Generate comprehensive tests for a file or module. Reads existing test patterns and matches the project's style. Covers happy paths, edge cases, error conditions, and boundary values.","headings":["Test Generation","Steps"],"name_hint":"测试","description_zh":"依据已有测试模式与项目风格，为文件模块生成覆盖正常、边缘、错误及边界值的测试。"},{"path":"skills/user-docs/SKILL.md","name":"user-docs","description":"Write user documentation for a project by scanning its codebase — its UI screens and its public API/CLI — inferring what someone can actually do with it, and drafting brief, task-oriented docs to the Diátaxis standard (tutorial / how-to / reference / explanation). Handles both non-technical end-user docs and developer docs. Use when asked to document the app, write user or API docs, generate a getting-started guide, or when the project's docs are missing or out of date. Scans and proposes an outline, then writes only after you approve it.","headings":["Write user documentation from the codebase","Argument","The standard","Steps","1. Find where docs live, and fit it","2. Build the capability inventory (the scan)","3. Propose the outline, then stop","4. Write the approved pages, one at a time","5. Verify","Don't"],"name_hint":"user · 文档","description_zh":"扫描项目UI与公共API/CLI推断真实用户任务，按Diátaxis教程操作参考解释标准起草简洁终端用户或开发者文档；先提纲，批准后写入。"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Clawness","Contents","Quickstart","Claude Code","OpenClaw (experimental)","What Problem Does This Solve?","How It Works","The retrieval engine","Install","Installing Python","Plugin install (recommended)","Manual install","Uninstall","macOS / Linux","Windows (PowerShell)","Using It","What your agent sees","MANDATORY (9)","RELEVANT (2)","Output compression","Context watch (Claude Code, on by default)","Session handoff (Claude Code, on by default)","Version-gap detection (on by default)","Plan gate (Claude Code, on by default)"]},{"path":"openclaw/README.md","headings":["Clawness for OpenClaw (experimental)","Install (experimental)","What works today (core scope)","Layout","Build & test"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".claude/settings.json",".clawness/memory.md",".editorconfig",".gitattributes",".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml",".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml",".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/feature_request.yml",".github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md",".github/workflows/ci.yml",".gitignore",".vscode/settings.json","CHANGELOG.md","CLAUDE.md","CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md","CONTRIBUTING.md","LICENSE","README.md","SECURITY.md","agents/arch-challenger.md","agents/code-critic.md","agents/perf-auditor.md","agents/refactor-advisor.md","agents/security-blue-team.md","agents/security-red-team.md","agents/test-writer.md","clawness/__init__.py","clawness/cli.py","clawness/context_watch.py","clawness/core.py","clawness/coverage.py","clawness/findings.py","clawness/guard.py","clawness/handoff.py","clawness/init.py","clawness/memory.py","clawness/model_advisor.py","clawness/plan.py","clawness/scan.py","clawness/session_state.py","clawness/staleness.py","clawness/trust.py","clawness/upgrade.py","hooks/_hookuti